<br/><!-- hnss:readable-content --><hr/><div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div>

  <div>
  	<p><span>Written by</span> @landaire<br>
  		<span>on&nbsp;</span><time datetime="2021-12-27">December 27, 2021</time>
  	</p>





        <p><a href="https://landaire.net/img/yaesu/ft70d.jpg"><img src="https://landaire.net/processed_images/485636b1e6ca756000.jpg"></a></p><p><em>This article dives into my full methodology for reverse engineering the tool mentioned in this article. It's a bit longer but is intended to be accessible to folks who aren't necessarily advanced reverse-engineers.</em></p>
<p><em>Click on any of the images to view at its original resolution.</em></p>




        <ul>

            <li>
